    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3aeaa933edb335fb0e6f6269b9b7f4f1c6b9f6e7b7af9eddf4e583ec859eee20",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The t-aspect and family recipes share a two-stage projection: Stirling phases in the shifted zeta calculation, or averaged root-number powers in a family, first restrict which approximate-functional-equation choices survive; coefficient orthogonality then imposes the relevant multiplicative diagonal, after which completion and Euler-product organization produce the conjectured main-term package.",
