    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_80782c772ff2b9f8d7a7a8d529e18cbc49f8f40af618fa7ad46fe4cc5593871d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Primewise factorization separates moment conjectures into a simple-pole skeleton and a regular arithmetic remainder: the first surviving local correlation layer determines whether poles occur between opposite blocks, only at distinct pairs, or also at self-pairs, while the residual Euler product retains the coefficients and ramified data specific to the underlying L-function or family.",
