      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The top-degree scaling limit of the full shifted residue splits into two independently computed factors: evaluating the analytic local Euler product at zero shifts recovers the arithmetic constant a_k, while the remaining Vandermonde contour is converted through gamma integrals and determinant/binomial manipulations into the universal symmetry constant g_k divided by k-squared factorial.",
